:: OC Micah Corner Store Siblings [nobr]

<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“But how are you supposed to watch the store all by yourself if you get scared every time someone raises their voice?”</span> A little voice says. Walking into the corner store, you see <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> standing at the register looking a little annoyed as a little boy sitting on the counter tossing a pack of gum into the air and catching it. The boy continues, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You gotta be more assertive, or everyone is just going to walk all over you and get discounts and stuff.”</span> <br>
<br>
<span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“It’s not <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span>’s fault!”</span> Another little voice says. You spot another short boy standing in one of the aisles moving some stuff around, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Not everyone can be super brave. Besides, teacher said that fear is good sometimes. People become cowards to protect themselves from danger, or something like that. So, it’s kinda good that he’s scared when people yell.”</span> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> groans loudly, lying his head on the counter. The other boy’s arguments were not helping. <br>
<br>
Upon suddenly seeing you standing there, <span style="color:Pink"> <span style="color:DarkTurquoise">Micah</span> turns bright red and quickly straighten up.</span> <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“Go- go to the back and play with your Blockz!”</span> He says, trying to shoo the little boys away, <span style="color:LightSteelBlue">“You know they don’t like you playing out here when we’re open. Go, go!”</span> He hurries them out into the back room before coming back and nervously chuckling. <br>

